{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My strength and my song — Yah.</b> The strength and song of the Holy One, blessed be He, <b>hurled into the sea</b> <b>horse and rider</b>, for by this He showed His strength — that He is King over all kings — and that it is fitting for those who are saved to praise Him with the voice of song, joyous to be servants to the King of the universe." "<b>And He was to me for salvation.</b> He who hurled the enemy into the sea was to me for salvation, as it says: וְנוֹדְעָה יַד ה׳ אֶת עֲבָדָיו / וְזָעַם אֶת אוֹיְבָיו (Isaiah 66:14)." "<b>This is my El.</b> He is the eternal and primordial One to me, to whom all causes of perishable beings must of necessity trace back, and from whom comes the eternity of their continued existence." "<b>And I will make Him a habitation.</b> I will make a habitation for His dwelling among us, and in it I will pray to Him alone and serve Him as is fitting for one who bestows good and responds to need, as it says: וַיִּתְפַּלֵּל אֵלָיו וַיֹּאמַר הַצִּילֵנִי כִּי אֵלִי אָתָּה (Isaiah 44:17) — for indeed worship and prayer are directed toward finding favor." "<b>The El of my father.</b> The El of Jacob, who made it known by saying אֵל אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Genesis 33:20) — that He is awesome in His greatness and in His providence, which are the attribute of mercy and the attribute of judgment." "<b>And I will exalt Him.</b> Through prostration and self-abasement, and by making known to all that the end aimed at — doing His will — is the best of all ends, since He is exalted above every blessing and praise, in the manner of לַמְּדֵנִי לַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנֶךָ כִּי אַתָּה אֱלוֹהָי (Psalms 143:10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:41.193897416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}